ult0 \f1\fs20{\b0\i0\cf1\charscalex84\expndtw8\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs31 Santiago   \b Write    to   Their}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\qc\li0\fi0\ri101\sb0\sa0\sl-293\slmult0 \f1\fs20{\b0\i0\cf1\charscalex87\expndtw4\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs30 Friends \b at Home.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\ql\li850\fi-811\ri0\sb355\sa0\sl-235\slmult0 \f1\fs20{\b\i0\cf1\charscalex100\expndtw4\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs19 GOOD     LETTER    IS    RECEIVED     FROM \expndtw0 PRIVATE   VANDENBOOM,}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\qc\li0\fi0\ri67\sb336\sa0\sl-274\slmult0 \f1\fs20{\b\i0\cf1\charscalex81\expndtw4\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs25 White Flag of Truce Was Flyine Over the Be-}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\qc\li0\fi0\ri43\sb0\sa0\sl-274\slmult0 \f1\fs20{\b\i0\cf1\charscalex86\expndtw6\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs23 leaeured City as He Wrote\loch\af0\hich\af0\dbch\f1\cchs0 \'97\hich\af0\dbch\af1\loch\f0\cchs0 Red Cross}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\qc\li0\fi0\ri48\sb0\sa0\sl-274\slmult0 \f1\fs20{\b0\i0\cf1\charscalex100\expndtw5\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Flags on Most of the Buildings}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\ql\li4061\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f1\fs20\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\ql\li1162\fi0\ri0\sb0\sa0 \f1\fs20{\b0\i0\cf1\charscalex100\expndtw2\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 Inside Fortifications.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\ql\li38\fi0\ri0\sb346\sa0 \f1\fs20{\b0\i0\cf1\charscalex100\expndtw9\f11\cchs0\lang1033\fs22 NEWS \b STRAIGHT FROM THE FRONT.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\qj\li38\fi192\ri101\sb24\sa0\sl-211\slmult0 \f1\fs20{\b0\i0\cf1\charscalex100\expndtw9\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs23 Several of the Marquette people who \expndtw14 have relatives and friends In Company \expndtw8 L were made happy when the mail man \expndtw10 came around yesterday, for he brought \expndtw13 them letters from the boys at the front.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\qj\li34\fi197\ri106\sb0\sa0\sl-211\slmult0\tx3504 \f1\fs20{\b0\i0\cf1\charscalex100\expndtw13\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs23 Letters are known to have been re\-\line \expndtw14 ceived from Lieutenant Wilson, Cor\-\line \expndtw8 poral Watson and Private Vandenboom.\line \expndtw9 All the letters were written as the boys\line \expndtw10 were lying in the trenches before San\-\line \expndtw0 tiago.{\charscalex100\expndtw0\tab }\super\cf9 v}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\qj\li24\fi197\ri91\sb0\sa0\sl-211\slmult0 \f1\fs20{\b0\i0\cf1\charscalex100\expndtw8\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs23 The chief hardship complained of is a \expndtw9 lack of letter paper. Corporal Watson's \expndtw14 letter and envelope is made up of the \expndtw9 same sheet. Private Vandenboom speaks \expndtw6 of "having found some paper." His in\-\expndtw7 teresting leter, which has been furnished \expndtw10 for publication, reads as follows:}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\qj\li29\fi192\ri48\sb0\sa0\sl-211\slmult0 \f1\fs20{\b0\i0\cf1\charscalex100\expndtw12\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs23 "I just found some paper, so I thought \expndtw13 I would set down and write a few lines \expndtw17 to let you know that I am right in. i.t,. \expndtw16 I am feeling good and looking good. I \expndtw10 tell you I am now right in the war field. \expndtw6 On the third the Spaniards stopped shoot\-\expndtw10 ing at noon and brought out their white \expndtw17 flag, so we put up ours. All day the \expndtw14 Fourth we didn't hear a shot, only a \expndtw17 scattered one once in a while. Maybe \expndtw8 you think the Spaniards ain't getttlng it. \expndtw6 July 2, about 11:30 at night, they sneaked \expndtw11 up over the hill and thought they were \expndtw18 going to have some fun with us. But \expndtw13 they got left. Our colored troops were \expndtw17 lying in their pits and the Spaniards \expndtw24 didn't know it. They were sneaking \expndtw13 up pretty close, when the boys opened \expndtw7 flre on them. Then about 2,000 of us \expndtw17 Volunteers jumped up and pitched in \expndtw14 and we didn't do a thing but get about \expndtw15 500, not any less. We only got a few \expndtw4 killed and a few wounded, amounting to \expndtw13 fifty-six all told. How is that for high? \expndtw15 Co. L is right in it. We are away down \expndtw8 in a hole and the Spaniards are in a hole \expndtw9 and a hill between us, and the colored \expndtw19 fellows are between us, so we got an A No. 1 place. We got guns all over \expndtw18 and old Sampson is in the harbor, all \expndtw5 O. K. Got in before midnight last night. \expndtw4 There are quite a \cf9 few \cf1 boys wounded and \expndtw9 quire \cf9 a \cf1 few killed. We are now getting \expndtw20 ready \cf9 for \cf1 bualnena again. It \cf9 Is \cf1 now \expndtw-12 6:30.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\qj\li77\fi192\ri115\sb0\sa0\sl-211\slmult0 \f1\fs20{\b0\i0\cf1\charscalex100\expndtw11\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs23 "Ed Blackwoocl has got the measle* \expndtw7 and Lieutenant Lelsen has got Inflam\-\expndtw15 mation of the lungs; too bad, but we \expndtw18 can't help \cf9 It. \cf1 I don't know how they \expndtw14 will pull through yet. but I hope they \expndtw20 will get \cf9 along \cf1 all right. I just heard \expndtw1 the Spaniards have got till 10 a.m. tomor\-\expndtw21 row, the 6th. They have got a Red \expndtw5 Cross on mostly every building in San\-\expndtw11 tiago; that looks bad for them. If they \expndtw6 don't surrender by 10 tomorrow we are \expndtw12 going to raise the Dickens with them, \expndtw6 and we are the boys who can do it, too. Well, I have to fall in now. Good morn\-\expndtw-6 ing.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\qj\li14\fi250\ri144\sb0\sa0\sl-211\slmult0 \f1\fs20{\b0\i0\cf1\charscalex100\expndtw15\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs23 "It is now the 6th. Everything was \expndtw21 quite last night; not a shot. I heard \expndtw3 this morning that Sampson wasn't In the \expndtw10 harbor and that he was scared to go in, but he has got to take chances. Every\-\expndtw7 body has a different story. I Just heard \expndtw12 again tha: the Spaniards have got ten \expndtw10 days more, but I don't believe In very \expndtw18 much what I hear around here. It is \expndtw9 quite warm down here, but then I don't feel any warmer than what I felt last \expndtw21 summer In the hay field. At night it \expndtw6 is quite cool; a person needs something \expndtw10 over him. The water we get down here \expndtw12 isn't very good; there are dead people \expndtw11 and horses in it, also mud, but we have \expndtw12 to drink something. L make quite a bit of coffee. I tell you I am quite a cook \expndtw7 now. I can cook mangoes right to per\-\expndtw17 fection. It is a fruit about the size of an orange. I make sauce out of them \expndtw14 and eat it on hard tack. CDld you get \expndtw18 any hard tack yet? And did you get \expndtw11 those pictures? If you didn't get them \expndtw12 about a dozen of us are going to string \expndtw10 up that gallery man, but I think he has \expndtw14 sent them by this time. We are now \expndtw11 located were we can't get a thing. The \expndtw8 only thing we can get Is hard tack, cof\-fee, a little sugar and pig and what fruit \expndtw16 we can find. Mangoes and cocoanuts \expndtw11 are all right, too.}\par \pard \plain \cbpat8\qj\li0\fi216\ri182\sb10\sa0\sl-211\slmult0 \f1\fs20{\b0\i0\cf1\charscalex100\expndtw11\f1\cchs0\lang1033\fs24 "It ia fun to see the mules come in \expndtw8 with big packs on their backs and they \expndtw3 all follow a horse with a big bell on. \expndtw4 Wherever the horse goes the mules are right there. The grass here Is about five \expndtw7 feet high. Well, I must fall In now and \expndtw3 get water."}\par }